description:
FOUND by s539d (#233) while probing caller(); PRE-EXISTING on main 05806e16 (probed on the extraction), unchanged by s539d.  SILENT WRONG (a diagnostic, and the target package of a caller-driven import).

    sub show { join "|", @_ }
    sub f11 { my @c = caller(0); print show(@c[0..3]), "\n" }
    my $obj = bless {}, 'K'; sub K::m { main::f11() } $obj->m;

    perl:  main|p.pl|3|main::f11
    PCL:   k|...|main::f11

TWO faces, ONE place: p-sub's per-sub constant %%home-pkg = (pcl-pkg-perl-name (symbol-package local-sym)), the package of the sub's NAME symbol.  (1) perl's code inside `sub K::m {...}` runs in the package it was COMPILED in (CopSTASH = main), not the package the name is installed in; (2) the CL package of a single-segment Perl package that no `package K;` statement ever named reads through :invert as "k", and *pcl-pkg-name-map* has no entry for it, so the case is lost too.  Fix shape: the emitter knows the compiling package of every `sub NAME` and could hand it to p-sub (a FACT, only on a QUALIFIED sub name, so a few bytes per such sub) -- measure.  Probe: s539d scratch pr/p1.pl row J.

=== MEASURED (s539d) -- the same cause holds 11 IO-Compress board rows ===
t/01misc.t's assertions run inside `sub My::testParseParameters() {...}` (compiled in main) and call `like $@, mkErr(...)`, a Test::More STRING pattern '/RE\s+at /'.  The TAP layer reads a string pattern as Test::More's maybe_regex only for a caller package that imported Test::More (cl/pcl-test.lisp %test-more-caller-p reads *pcl-current-package*), and inside that sub *pcl-current-package* is "My" -- so the string is read as test.pl's literal-ish pattern and the row fails although the croak text now carries perl's ` at FILE line N.` (s539d).  Probe (perl: 3 ok; base and tree: rows 1 and 3 fail):

    use Test::More tests => 3;
    my $e = "x got 1 at - line 0.\n";
    sub My::t1() { like $e, "/got 1\\s+at /", "in My::t1" }  sub t2() { like $e, "/got 1\\s+at /", "in t2" }
    My::t1(); t2();  sub My::t3() { like $e, '/got 1\s+at /', "My::t3" } My::t3();

The 11 rows of 01misc.t (4-11, 14-16) were re-keyed from NS:ns-error-location to #4941 by s539d.  The fix is this task's (the compiling package as the sub's home), not the TAP layer's.
